D04 -- DOES FALSIFIER ROW 11 TEST THE FRAMEWORK'S LAW?  G158's slope channel, run on the law itself.
========================================================================================================
Row 11 ('the n-kill', G158) is registered FIRED: the deep slope beta, mapped by the task-declared rule n = 2*beta,
reads n = 1.20 +/- 0.06, '12.7 sigma from 2.000'.  In the programme's own family the seesaw n is an AMPLITUDE
(a0 = s/n) and the deep slope is 1/2 for every n; the rule n = 2*beta gives the canonical footing beta = 1, the
Newtonian slope.  Here the lane's own estimator is run on data that obey the law exactly.
Law under test: the TASK-DECLARED curve g = a0 (g_N/a0)^(n/2)  [MUTATE control].
Footings: canonical a0 = 9.3619e-11 (seesaw n = 2.000), alternative a0 = 1.1279e-10 (n = 1.660).
Run from the repository root:  python3 real_research/reviews/deep_a0eff_audit_2026_09_25/D04_g158_slope_channel.py

