DIAGNOSIS  (added after the first run, in which I1 and P1 failed as pre-stated; changes no pre-stated result and not the exit code)
======================================================================================================================
  (1) G158's per-galaxy error is the spread of THREE sample values (numpy std, which divides by 3, then /sqrt 3).  Read as the
      lane's own error model, its 'sigma' is a t statistic with 2 degrees of freedom, inflated by sqrt(3/2): the committed 12.7
      is t = 10.40, two-sided p = 0.0091, 2.61 sigma Gaussian-equivalent; its firing line '3 sigma' has a
      false-alarm rate of 13.4 per cent, not 0.27.  (Against beta = 1 the paired bootstrap of D gives 6.0-6.9 sigma: P1.)
  (2) the same injections with G158's OWN mapped null exactly true (beta = n/2 = 1 at n = 2) against the framework's law exactly true:
      committed    fires   7.0% /   7.8% (per-galaxy / ring level) when beta = 1 is true;    6.5% /   7.5% when the law is true
      std05_cut    fires   6.5% /  14.5% (per-galaxy / ring level) when beta = 1 is true;    3.2% /  16.8% when the law is true
      std06_cut    fires   4.5% /  12.5% (per-galaxy / ring level) when beta = 1 is true;    2.8% /  14.8% when the law is true
      std07_cut    fires   4.5% /  12.0% (per-galaxy / ring level) when beta = 1 is true;    3.2% /  14.2% when the law is true
      std05_nocut  fires   5.0% /  13.8% (per-galaxy / ring level) when beta = 1 is true;    5.2% /  11.2% when the law is true
      the firing separates beta = 1 from beta = 1/2.  It says nothing about n = 2.000 against n = 1.660, and its rate on its own null
      is the lane's real false-alarm rate.
